WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.640
The mean is what everyone would have if the total

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:03.650
were shared equally.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.520
So a mean always hides a total: the mean multiplied by

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:08.450
the number of items.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.350
Whenever a question mentions an average,

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:12.810
recover the total first.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:15.330
When groups have different sizes,

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.370
their averages carry different weight.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:20.530
Recover the total in each group before combining them.

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:23.710
Then each individual item makes the right contribution.

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:26.720
Four scores have a mean of seven.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:30.060
A fifth score is added and the mean becomes eight.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:31.680
What is the fifth score?

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:33.480
Pause and find the totals.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:39.970
Four scores with mean seven total twenty-eight.

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.120
Five scores with mean eight total forty.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.610
The fifth score supplies the difference:

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.830
forty minus twenty-eight is twelve.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.860
To average eight, the original four scores would

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:52.130
need thirty-two points.

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:55.650
They have twenty-eight, so they are four points short.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:58.980
The fifth score supplies its own eight points and those

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:00.190
four extra points.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:03.230
Combining groups works the same way.

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:06.650
Two people average six and three people average ten.

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:08.910
The totals are twelve and thirty,

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.290
forty-two for five people.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.610
The combined mean is eight point four, not eight.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:16.710
It leans towards the larger group.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:20.590
Order the five values: two, three, five,

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:21.870
nine and thirty-one.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:24.610
The middle value, five, is the median.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.230
Their sum is fifty, so the mean is ten.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:29.030
Now take away the five.

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:32.300
Four values remain, with three and nine in the

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:33.310
two middle positions.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.870
For an even number of values, average those middle two.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.070
Three plus nine is twelve.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:41.750
Half of twelve is six, the new median.

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:44.190
A mean lets you rebuild a total.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.770
For a median, put the values in order.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:49.030
Use the middle value if there is one,

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:50.670
or average the middle two.

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:54.450
Notebook challenge: the mean of six numbers is nine.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:57.970
One number is removed and the mean of the rest is eight.

00:01:58.620 --> 00:01:59.670
Which number was removed?
